---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/segmentation";
const title = "Shopify email apps for segmentation: workflow guide";
const desc = "Turn audience rules into explainable, maintained decisions.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Are tags enough?",
    "answer": "Tags can carry useful explicit state, but each needs an owner, update rule and removal rule. Compare their behavior with the decision you need."
  },
  {
    "question": "How many segments should I maintain?",
    "answer": "Maintain the definitions with a real consumer and a manageable review process. Store revenue or a fixed segment count is not a universal limit."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does overlap mean something is wrong?",
    "answer": "No. Overlap becomes a problem when it causes conflicting messages, duplicate counts or inconsistent benefits."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Segmentation</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email apps for segmentation: workflow guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Turn audience rules into explainable, maintained decisions.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Write the action before the filter</h2>
      <p>A segment needs a job: choose relevant content, qualify an offer, pause a workflow or identify a service task. Write the action and owner before building the audience; a saved filter without a consumer adds maintenance without a decision.</p>
      <p>Start with the decisions you actually make. Buyers versus prospects may support welcome routing; purchased category may support product education. Neither requires a universal list of eight segments or a maximum segment count.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Define each field precisely</h2>
      <p>Specify whether spend is lifetime or rolling, gross or net of returns, and in which currency. Define which order states count. Capture timezone, time boundary and whether multiple orders on the same day count separately.</p>
      <p>Record field source, refresh interval and null behavior. An absent order history can mean a new customer or an incomplete import. Treat unknown as a distinct state until you can establish which it is.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Separate eligibility from permission</h2>
      <p>An audience can match a commercial rule while lacking permission for a channel. Keep email eligibility, SMS eligibility and operational exclusions separate from product affinity and value labels.</p>
      <p>Do not make a purchase, a checkout address or an ad audience match stand in for marketing permission. Ad exports need their own approved purpose and field scope; importing membership back should not restore an email suppression.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Use declared and observed interest carefully</h2>
      <p>A customer’s stated preference, quiz response and purchased item describe different things. Save their source and date rather than combining them into an unexplained interest tag. A gift purchase may say little about personal preference.</p>
      <p>Check coverage before adding a branch. If few profiles have a usable shade or pet profile, build a useful unknown path and an optional preference update. Avoid inferring sensitive traits from category visits.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose live membership or a snapshot</h2>
      <p>Live audiences are useful for changing eligibility; campaign snapshots support review and reproducible reporting. Record when each was evaluated, and recheck critical exclusions at send time even when the creative audience was frozen earlier.</p>
      <p>Late order events can arrive after queue entry. Define how a new purchase removes an obsolete offer, and what happens when the data source is unavailable. A stale timestamp should be visible to the operator.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Resolve overlap at the message level</h2>
      <p>Multiple memberships are normal: a VIP can also have a cart and need a replenishment reminder. Decide which actual messages conflict and whether to pause, combine or skip them. Do not treat any overlap percentage as proof of failure.</p>
      <p>Document each collision with its reason, owner and resume rule. Essential order information needs separate handling from promotional frequency. A fixed hierarchy for every store can hide a promised welcome benefit or a time-sensitive launch invitation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Make membership explainable</h2>
      <p>For a sampled profile, show which predicates passed and which excluded it. Review boundary cases just below and above spend thresholds, a return, a null field, a merged identity and a late order. These are proposed validation records.</p>
      <p>Compare counts with the source system for the same time and definition. Trace differences to event delays, currency conversion, order-state handling or identity joins before changing the filter to make totals look similar.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Give definitions a lifecycle</h2>
      <p>Keep a register of identifier, purpose, owner, source fields, consumers, version and last review. Archive unused definitions only after finding their campaign, automation and reporting consumers.</p>
      <p>Review when catalogs, capture forms or integrations change. Retain prior definitions for historical reporting; changing membership logic mid-report otherwise makes before-and-after audience performance hard to interpret.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Measure a decision rather than a label</h2>
      <p>Track coverage, unknown values, refresh lag and incorrect enrollments. Commercial reporting should compare equivalent eligibility windows and count a customer once where audience totals overlap.</p>
      <p>High revenue per recipient in a high-value segment does not establish that segmentation caused the revenue. Propose a suitable randomized comparison for a messaging decision, or describe observational differences without causal claims.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Select and migrate with actual predicates</h2>
      <p>Ask a provider to recreate one complex filter, show a member’s inclusion reason, update a refund and suppress a queued message after a new order. Verify field mapping and supported operators in current primary documentation before selecting a plan.</p>
      <p>Rebuild definitions against authoritative records rather than importing every old tag as truth. Preserve consent, exclusions and version history, compare sample membership, then switch consumers deliberately. Include connectors, storage, sends and maintenance in cost comparisons.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><a class="link" href="/use-cases/segmentation">Audience definitions →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">Post-purchase →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch →</a></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Segmentation FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
